  "question": {
    "text": "Stearic acid and polyethylene glycol react to form which one of the following soap/s detergents?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Cationic detergent",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Soap",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Anionic detergent",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Non-ionic detergent",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>&nbsp;Non-ionic detergents do not contain any ion in their constitution. One such detergent is formed when stearic acid reacts with polyethylene glycol.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><mrow><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>16</mn></msub><mi>COOH</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>Stearic</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>acid</mi></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><mrow><mi>HO</mi><msub><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></msub><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>OH</mi></mrow><mi>Polyethyleneglycol</mi></munder><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mover><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>16</mn></msub><mi>COO</mi><msub><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></msub><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>OH</mi></math></p><p>&nbsp;A&nbsp;type of detergent in which the active part of the molecule is a positive ion (cation). Cationic detergents are usually quaternary ammonium salts.</p><p>Anionic detergent is a synthetic detergent in which a lipophilic hydrocarbon group of the molecule is an anion. A detergent molecule consists of a long hydrocarbon chain and a water-soluble negative ionic group.</p></blockquote>"
